show/134789712.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/m23-guerrillas-wars-shadow-economy-how-congos-militias-turn-guns-gold-and-tolls-into-profit/articleshow/134789712.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:11:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134790953,imgsize-156172.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From France to Italy, Belgium to Greece, student protests spread across Europe]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134785388.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The movement began in the Paris region in mid-September, when high-school students and teachers protested over a lack of resources and staff. It quickly spread across France, with students blocking school entrances and later joined by university students, parents and trade unions. Their complaints include overcrowded classrooms, teachers not being replaced when absent, long school hours, deteriorating buildings and inequalities between schools in wealthier and poorer areas.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/from-france-to-italy-belgium-to-greece-student-protests-spread-across-europe/articleshow/134785388.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/from-france-to-italy-belgium-to-greece-student-protests-spread-across-europe/articleshow/134785388.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:34:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791439,imgsize-226388.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Israel-Britain ties hit new low as Jerusalem consulate loses diplomatic status]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791840.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Britain and Israel continue to cooperate closely on defence and security, but their wider diplomatic relationship has deteriorated over Israel's conduct of the war against Hamas in Gaza and Britain's decision last year to recognise a Palestinian state. The dispute over the consulate comes against the backdrop of the wider Israeli-Palestinian conflict.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-britain-ties-hit-new-low-as-jerusalem-consulate-loses-its-diplomatic-status/articleshow/134791840.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-britain-ties-hit-new-low-as-jerusalem-consulate-loses-its-diplomatic-status/articleshow/134791840.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:48:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791957,imgsize-244030.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NSW protects first pink lakes: governments buy Pulgamurtie Station]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134788892.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The acquisition of Pulgamurtie Station in New South Wales, covering 74,000 hectares of unique landscapes, aims to protect the area's stunning pink lakes and vulnerable wildlife. This initiative not only prioritizes Aboriginal cultural heritage but also fosters diverse ecosystems vital for local species. Future plans include opportunities for recreational activities like birdwatching and scenic drives, supporting Australia's goal to expand protected areas.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/nsw-and-australian-governments-buy-74000-hectare-outback-station-protecting-states-first-pink-lakes-and-habitat-for-70-threatened-species-including-brolga-pink-cockatoo-and-slender-darling-pea/articleshow/134788892.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/nsw-and-australian-governments-buy-74000-hectare-outback-station-protecting-states-first-pink-lakes-and-habitat-for-70-threatened-species-including-brolga-pink-cockatoo-and-slender-darling-pea/articleshow/134788892.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T17:06:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134789073,imgsize-167750.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Egypt arrests 6 journalists from fact-checking website over ‘terrorism’, ‘fake news’ charges]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134790361.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egypt-arrests-6-journalists-from-fact-checking-website-over-terrorism-fake-news-charges/articleshow/134790361.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egypt-arrests-6-journalists-from-fact-checking-website-over-terrorism-fake-news-charges/articleshow/134790361.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:01:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134790695,imgsize-80356.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[John Paul DeJoria’s Texas ranch sold for $6.93 million; 120 exotic animals included]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134790028.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable real estate deal, the sprawling Texas ranch of Patrón Tequila co-founder John Paul 