p-administration/articleshow/134788569.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T16:55:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134788592,imgsize-48102.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Stanford’s 20-year blood-cancer therapy treats first commercial patient; trial found 78% free of GVHD]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134788057.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable advancement, Stanford researchers have unveiled Orca-T therapy, which has recently received FDA approval. After two decades of rigorous development, this innovative treatment was administered to its inaugural commercial patient, a high-risk leukemia sufferer. Notably, Orca-T significantly minimizes the chances of graft-versus-host disease post-stem cell transplants, offering reduced chemotherapy requirements and lower side effects. Future studies are anticipated to investigate its relevance for broader patient demographics.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/stanford-spent-more-than-20-years-developing-a-blood-cancer-transplant-therapy-its-first-commercial-patient-has-now-been-treated-after-a-trial-found-78-were-free-from-moderate-to-severe-gvhd-at-one-year/articleshow/134788057.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/stanford-spent-more-than-20-years-developing-a-blood-cancer-transplant-therapy-its-first-commercial-patient-has-now-been-treated-after-a-trial-found-78-were-free-from-moderate-to-severe-gvhd-at-one-year/articleshow/134788057.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134788220,imgsize-1937327.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[DoorDash driver in Maryland crashes during delivery, still arranges for customer to collect food]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134784880.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A DoorDash driver in Maryland, US, survived a serious crash after his car's brakes failed during a delivery. Despite the accident, he told his customer where to collect the food. The customer's video of the unusual pickup went viral, drawing attention to the driver's financial difficulties. An online fundraiser later raised over $16,000 to help him recover.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-maryland-doordash-drivers-brakes-failed-and-his-car-was-totalled-during-a-delivery-yet-he-still-told-the-customer-where-to-collect-the-food-the-video-went-viral-and-his-fundraiser-later-climbed-past-15000/articleshow/134784880.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-maryland-doordash-drivers-brakes-failed-and-his-car-was-totalled-during-a-delivery-yet-he-still-told-the-customer-where-to-collect-the-food-the-video-went-viral-and-his-fundraiser-later-climbed-past-15000/articleshow/134784880.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T16:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134785332,imgsize-56506.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Let them hit Los Angeles’: Trump clarifies Iran war remarks, says he ‘won’t let that happen’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134788618.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/news/let-them-hit-los-angeles-trump-clarifies-iran-war-remarks-says-he-wont-let-that-happen/articleshow/1